0.02.127.262 W common_fit_params:   a placement can buy the KV back -- --fit will not take it on your behalf:
0.02.127.263 W common_fit_params:     --kv-window N            keep the newest N cells of the attention KV in VRAM and the
0.02.127.264 W common_fit_params:                             older ones in pinned system RAM (ONE copy, LOSSLESS, any model).
0.02.127.264 W common_fit_params:                             Costs decode in proportion to the depth past N, and nothing when
0.02.127.264 W common_fit_params:                             N is at or above your run depth;
0.02.127.264 W common_fit_params:                             `--kv-window auto` lets this fit choose N for the -c you pinned.
0.02.127.264 W common_fit_params:   it changes no token (ENVIRONMENT.md 17).  Lowering -c, -ngl or the quant also fits, and
0.02.127.265 W common_fit_params:   always ends in a clean refusal rather than an allocator abort.
